  <div class="container py-5">
    <p style="max-width: 50rem;">
      Mainstream Knowledge Graphs (KGs) often assume a monolithic notion of truth,
      offering limited support for context-dependent validity, conflicting viewpoints,
      knowledge evolution, and concept drift. This full-day <i>Barstuhl</i> workshop introduces
      <strong>Multi-dimensional Knowledge Graphs (MKGs)</strong> as an umbrella paradigm for contextual,
      perspectival, and temporal knowledge representation. The main outcome is a
      community-driven framework document that will serve as the foundation for an
      MKG white paper and a potential future Dagstuhl seminar.
    </p>

