    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Research questions &amp; engineering challenges</h2>
      <p class="lead mb-4" style="max-width: 48rem;">
        Two interlocking tracks &mdash; formal foundations and computational engineering &mdash;
        frame the workshop's breakout sessions.
      </p>

      <ul class="nav nav-pills nav-pills-mkg mb-4" id="research-tabs" role="tablist">
        <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
          <button class="nav-link active" id="tab-foundational" data-bs-toggle="tab"
            data-bs-target="#pane-foundational" type="button" role="tab"
            aria-controls="pane-foundational" aria-selected="true">Foundational track</button>
        </li>
        <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
          <button class="nav-link" id="tab-computational" data-bs-toggle="tab"
            data-bs-target="#pane-computational" type="button" role="tab"
            aria-controls="pane-computational" aria-selected="false">Computational track</button>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="tab-content">
        <div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="pane-foundational" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-foundational">
          <div class="row g-3">
            <div class="col-md-4">
              <div class="card-mkg border-wg-a">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <span class="wg-badge wg-a mb-2">RQ1 &middot; Formal foundations</span>
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0">What minimal, sound formalisms can natively represent
                    multi-dimensional assertions (time, perspective, stance) while
                    preserving W3C backward compatibility?</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
              <div class="card-mkg border-wg-a">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <span class="wg-badge wg-a mb-2">RQ2 &middot; Epistemological alignment</span>
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0">How can we align divergent, contradictory dimensions or
                    conflicting ontologies within the same graph without triggering logical
                    inconsistency?</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
              <div class="card-mkg border-wg-a">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <span class="wg-badge wg-a mb-2">RQ3 &middot; Concept drift</span>
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0">What formalisms let a model track and query the
                    historical evolution of a concept's meaning over time without schema
                    fragmentation?</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pane-computational" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-computational">
          <div class="row g-3">
            <div class="col-md-4">
              <div class="card-mkg border-wg-b">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <span class="wg-badge wg-b mb-2">EC1 &middot; Query &amp; storage</span>
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0">How should query languages, storage models, and
                    indexing strategies evolve to efficiently support querying over multiple
                    contextual dimensions?</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
              <div class="card-mkg border-wg-b">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <span class="wg-badge wg-b mb-2">EC2 &middot; Scalable evolution</span>
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0">How can storage engines efficiently manage temporal
                    evolution, concept drift, and multiple graph versions without excessive
                    data duplication or query overhead?</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
              <div class="card-mkg border-wg-c">
                <div class="card-body">
                  <span class="wg-badge wg-c mb-2">EC3 &middot; Interoperability &amp; AI</span>
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0">How can multi-dimensional KGs provide a scalable
                    symbolic foundation for neuro-symbolic AI, Retrieval-Augmented
                    Generation, and other AI systems while preserving contextual
                    semantics?</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4" style="max-width: 48rem;">
